Changes, made on 2026-10-26: the Lean files keep CompCert's names and only the definitions that the
semantics of this directory uses, without proof fields.  Machine integers are Lean's fixed-width
words, floating-point numbers are their bit patterns, and the numerical results of floating-point
operations come from Talos's integer implementation of IEEE 754 instead of Flocq, with NaN results
computed as Floats.v computes them.  Block contents are tree maps, and the parameters of x86-64 and
AArch64 that both targets share are fixed.  Rules for constructs outside the translator's subset
are omitted, and each file's documentation comment lists what it omits.  The other files of
LeanExe/Native/ are not derived from CompCert.

Changes, made on 2026-10-27: AST.lean gains type_of_chunk, Globalenvs.lean find_var_info and
block_is_volatile, Events.lean eventval_match without the case of pointers, volatile_load,
volatile_load_sem, volatile_store, and volatile_store_sem, with the cases EF_vload and EF_vstore
of external_call, and Bigstep.lean the judgment about a whole program,
bigstep_program_terminates.  external_call takes the global environment, where
CompCert takes a symbol environment, and passes its symbol map to the parameter of external
functions as before.
